{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/732","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:48.262616+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Thanks for catching this.\r\n\r\nI verified that this only happens with jax_enable_x64 switched on. I believe this is a Python scalars issue (which our tests don't cover).","created_at":"2019-05-19T15:45:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/732#issuecomment-493767958","id":493767958,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/732","minimized":null,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5Mzc2Nzk1OA==","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":1,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/493767958/reactions"},"updated_at":"2019-05-19T15:45:31Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/493767958","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1458824?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattjj","id":1458824,"login":"mattjj","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTg4MjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"The problem is that [we follow NumPy's special treatment of builtin numeric types in our type promotion logic](https://github.com/google/jax/blob/bb5cbaabaab033a78107987309161041cfa1780b/jax/numpy/lax_numpy.py#L147-L162), but that only works for literals and not argument values passed to`@jit`  functions because we don't have a special abstract value for Python scalars and thus we lose the information we'd need to give them special treatment.\r\n\r\nThere are at least two things we could want here:\r\n1. follow NumPy\r\n2. don't change behavior when applying `@jit`\r\n\r\nI think the latter is more important than the former. Moreover a heavyweight solution to achieve both probably isn't worth the added complexity, so whenever the two in tension, we should choose the latter.\r\n\r\nMy current understanding of this issue is that it shows the code is currently achieving some cases of (1) at the expense of (2). We should consider re-prioritizing.\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, one thing you can do is just not pass Python scalars as arguments. That's unfortunately made slightly trickier by #121, since you can't just write `c = np.array(0.1)` here; you have to write `c = onp.array(0.1)` until we fix #121.","created_at":"2019-05-19T19:43:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/732#issuecomment-493785774","id":493785774,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/732","minimized":null,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ5Mzc4NTc3NA==","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/493785774/reactions"},"updated_at":"2019-05-20T00:06:05Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/493785774","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1458824?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattjj/following{/oth